+\section{Entire-function diagnostics}
+\label{sec:diagnostics}
+
+For each accepted eigenvalue we will compute the coefficient sequence with
+certified tail diagnostics and evaluate $\psi$ on expanding compact subsets of
+$\C$.  The main observables are
+\begin{equation}
+  \log_{10}|\psi(z)|,
+  \qquad \arg\psi(z),
+  \qquad \{z\in\C:\psi(z)=0\}.
+\end{equation}
+Plots on finite windows must be accompanied by convergence checks under both
+series-order and domain enlargement.  Analytic growth estimates will be used
+to distinguish global statements about the entire function from finite-window
+numerics.
+
+\section{Iterated-function experiment}
+\label{sec:iteration}
+
+As a separate complex-dynamical experiment, define
+\begin{equation}
+  z_{j+1}=\psi(z_j).
+\end{equation}
+Escape-time and basin plots may reveal intricate structures.  Their dependence
+on eigenfunction normalization and units must be displayed explicitly; this
+iteration is not the Schr\"odinger or Lindblad time evolution of the cavity.
+
+\section{Numerical validation plan}
+
+The computational implementation will test recurrence residuals, Bargmann
+norm convergence, stability under precision and truncation changes, and zero
+locations via the argument principle.  Direct diagonalization may be retained
+as an independent check, but not as the defining spectral method.
